{title: O Little Town of Bethlehem}
{artist: Phillips Brooks & Lewis Redner}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[F]O little town of [Bb]Bethle[F]hem, how [Dm]still we [C]see thee [F]lie!
Above thy deep and [Bb]dreamless [F]sleep the [Dm]silent [C]stars go [F]by;
yet in thy dark streets [A]shineth the [Dm]everlasting [C]Light —
the [F]hopes and fears of [Bb]all the [F]years are [Dm]met in [C]thee to[F]night.

Verse 2
[F]For Christ is born [Bb]of Mary, [Dm]and gathered [C]all above, [F]While
mortals sleep, the angels [Bb]keep [F]their [Dm]watch [C]of wond'ring [F]love.
O morning stars together, [A]proclaim the [Dm]holy [C]birth, And
praises [F]sing to God the [Bb]King, [F]and peace [Dm]to men [C]on earth!

Verse 3
[F]How silently, how silently, [Bb]the wondrous [Dm]Gift is [C]giv'n; So [F]God
imparts to human hearts [Bb]the [F]blessings of [Dm]His [C]Heav'n. No [F]ear
may hear His coming, but [A]in this [Dm]world [C]of sin,
Where [F]meek souls will receive [Bb]Him [F]still, the [Dm]dear Christ [C]enters in.

Verse 4
[F]Where children pure [F]and happy [Dm]pray [C]to [F]the
blessèd Child, Where [Bb]misery [F]cries out to [Dm]Thee, [C]Son of [F]the
mother mild; Where charity stands watching and [A]faith holds [Dm]wide the [C]door,
The [F]dark night wakes, [Bb]the glory [F]breaks, and [Dm]Christmas [C]comes once [F]more.

Verse 5
[F]O holy Child of [Bb]Bethlehem, descend [Dm]to us, [C]we pray; [F]Cast
out our sin, and [Bb]enter [F]in, [Dm]be [C]born in [F]us
today. We hear the [A]Christmas angels [Dm]the [C]great glad
tidings [F]tell; O come to [Bb]us, [F]abide with [Dm]us, our [C]Lord Emmanuel!
